AIM:
To return the index of the first occurrence of needle in haystack.
If needle exists in haystack, return its starting index.
If not, return -1.
JAVA CODE:
public class FirstOccurrence {
    public static int strStr(String haystack, String needle) {
        // Use built-in indexOf for simplicity
        return haystack.indexOf(needle);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Example 1
        String haystack1 = "sadbutsad";
        String needle1 = "sad";
        System.out.println(strStr(haystack1, needle1)); // Output: 0

        // Example 2
        String haystack2 = "leetcode";
        String needle2 = "leeto";
        System.out.println(strStr(haystack2, needle2)); // Output: -1
    }
}
INPUT:
haystack = "sadbutsad"
needle = "sad"
OUTPUT:
0
